# Do not hard-reload the browser from the agent

Do **not** hard-reload the Cursor-owned HA tab. CDP `Page.reload` with `ignoreCache`, Ctrl+Shift+R / Cmd+Shift+R, “empty cache and hard refresh”, or opening a **new** Cursor browser tab to force a fresh `panel.js` / custom element can reload the **whole Cursor window**.

## Do this instead

- Pick up new `panel.js` by bumping `PANEL_ASSET_REV` in `panel.py` and `docker compose restart`. The versioned asset URL is the cache-bust — see [`docs/DECISIONS.md`](../../docs/DECISIONS.md).
- Keep using the **already-open** sandbox tab.
- In-page Home Assistant navigation is fine (sidebar, hash routes, `browser_navigate` to an HA URL).
- A **normal** refresh is often **required** after a rev bump: `location.reload()` (no `ignoreCache`), or the user hitting reload. Soft hash-only navigation frequently keeps the old `circadian-scenes-panel` custom element registered, so you can still be looking at pre-restart JS.
- After reload, **verify the new build** before debugging layout (shadow DOM / CSS marker for your change, or absence of removed nodes). Wait until HA finishes startup (“Wrapping up startup…”) — early loads 404 or show a spinner.
- Landscape checks: CDP `Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride` (wide × short) + `resize` / `_syncYearScrubLayout()`; pierce shadow to find `circadian-scenes-panel`.

Prefer measuring the already-open sandbox tab after a restart plus a normal document reload.
